WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.273
The 8085 is an eight-bit microprocessor with an accumulator, general-purpose registers, flags, a program counter and a stack pointer.

00:00:09.273 --> 00:00:17.082
Register roles matter when reading assembly: instructions describe transfers and operations on these named storage locations.

00:00:17.082 --> 00:00:20.010
The model is historical and educational.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.739
A contains 2AH after the first instruction.

00:00:23.739 --> 00:00:28.027
MOV copies that value into B, so both registers contain 2AH.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:31.535
Copying a register value does not erase the source.

00:00:32.535 --> 00:00:34.898
Which register is the accumulator?

00:00:34.898 --> 00:00:37.260
The accumulator is register A.
